    "sbar": {
      "situation": "The incident is recovered: the last two recovery checks ran clean, and the payment journey now completes. The incident commander reverted the gateway and payments settings itself, and failed screening over to its standby.",
      "background": "The pipeline changed payments max_transfer_minor from 1000000 to 1 about 14 seconds before the incident was handled, and payments began rejecting transfers above 1 minor unit. Ops-maintenance changed gateway balance_cache_ttl_s from 0.5 to 600.0 about 40 seconds earlier, so the gateway served stale balances. Screening exited with code 15 and was not answering.",
      "assessment": "Three root causes were found: bad_config on payments (confidence 0.95), process_down on screening (confidence 0.9), and bad_config on gateway (confidence 0.9). The incident commander reverted payments max_transfer_minor to 1000000 and gateway balance_cache_ttl_s to 0.5 by hand. It also failed screening over to its standby and restarted screening. All four actions reported done.",
      "recommendation": "Confirm the payment journey stays clean and watch screening, since it crashed twice in 15 minutes and is still served by its standby. Have the operations team review the balance mismatch: the app showed 99999900 while the ledger held 99999600 during the stale-cache window, and any payments rejected at the 1-unit limit need reconciliation. Investigate why the pipeline and ops-maintenance changed these settings, and why the gateway cache TTL was raised."
